**Current support versus accepted design.** Today `config.moth` uses declaration-owned `#Config of T` inputs with parenthesised grouped `project` and `html` records. `$project`, `$html_builder` and a required `version` argument are accepted queued design. `moth new` does not yet emit them. See @../progress (Progress).

`config.moth` at the project root controls build settings. It is one self-contained compile-time source file with no source dependencies.

### Accepted starter

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    $config
    version #String = "0.1.0"

    $project(
        name = "my_site",
        version = version,
        entry_root = "src",
    )

    $html_builder
]

`version` is required on `$project`. The `"0.1.0"` default belongs to the example `$config` contract, not to `$project`. Passing `version = version` is explicit; the name match alone is not enough.

`$html_builder` configures the already selected HTML builder. Bare `$html_builder` uses defaults. Empty parentheses are invalid.

### Current grouped config

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    version #Config of String = "0.1.0"

    project #= (
        name = "my_project",
        version = version,
        entry_root = "src",
    )

    html #= (
        dev_output = "dev",
        release_output = "release",
    )
]
